.* QTOCTBL: WRKSRVTBLE, WRKPCLTBLE and WRKNETTBLE (CFGTCP option 21's
.* tables). Each has a panel with every option and one with 5=Display
.* only. A one-column spacer puts the protocol and network names where
.* the system shows them.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 255'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=PORTCL BASETYPE='BIN 31'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=PCLCL BASETYPE='CHAR 26'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=SVNAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 32'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=PCNAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 32'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NTNAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 35'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NBRCL BASETYPE='BIN 31'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=ADRCL BASETYPE='CHAR 15'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=SPCL BASETYPE='CHAR 1'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=SP CLASS=SPCL.
:VAR NAME=SVCNAME CLASS=SVNAMECL.
:VAR NAME=SVCPORT CLASS=PORTCL.
:VAR NAME=SVCPROTO CLASS=PCLCL.
:VAR NAME=PCLNAME CLASS=PCNAMECL.
:VAR NAME=PCLNBR CLASS=NBRCL.
:VAR NAME=NETNAME CLASS=NTNAMECL.
:VAR NAME=NETADR CLASS=ADRCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=SVCS VARS='OPT SVCNAME SVCPORT SVCPROTO'.
:LISTDEF NAME=PCLS VARS='OPT SP PCLNAME PCLNBR'.
:LISTDEF NAME=NETS VARS='OPT SP NETNAME NETADR'.
:KEYL NAME=WRKKEYS HELP='KEYS/WRKKEYS'.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F6 ACTION='RETURN 6'.F6=Print list
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION='RETURN 17'.F17=Top
:KEYI KEY=F18 ACTION='RETURN 18'.F18=Bottom
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKSRV HELP=HLPSRV KEYL=WRKKEYS ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Work with Service Table Entries
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=SVCS SCROLL=YES ACTLEN=1 EXTACT=YES.(No entries in table)
:LISTACT OPTION=1 ACTFOR=EXTACT ENTER='CMD ?ADDSRVTBLE SERVICE(''&SVCNAME.'') PORT(&SVCPORT.) PROTOCOL(''&SVCPROTO.'')' HELP='WRKSRV/OPTIONS'.1=Add
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD RMVSRVTBLE SERVICE(''&SVCNAME.'') PORT(&SVCPORT.) PROTOCOL(''&SVCPROTO.'')' HELP='WRKSRV/OPTIONS'.4=Remove
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='RETURN 105' HELP='WRKSRV/OPTIONS'.5=Display
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='WRKSRV/OPT'.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=SVCNAME USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES HELP='FLD/SVCNAME'.Service
:LISTCOL VAR=SVCPORT USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES HELP='FLD/SVCPORT'.Port
:LISTCOL VAR=SVCPROTO USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES HELP='FLD/SVCPROTO'.Protocol
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters for options 1 and 4 or command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKSRVD HELP=HLPSRV KEYL=WRKKEYS ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Work with Service Table Entries
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=SVCS SCROLL=YES ACTLEN=1 EXTACT=YES.(No entries in table)
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='RETURN 105' HELP='WRKSRVD/OPTIONS'.5=Display
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='WRKSRVD/OPT'.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=SVCNAME USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES HELP='FLD/SVCNAME'.Service
:LISTCOL VAR=SVCPORT USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES HELP='FLD/SVCPORT'.Port
:LISTCOL VAR=SVCPROTO USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES HELP='FLD/SVCPROTO'.Protocol
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters for options 1 and 4 or command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKPCL HELP=HLPPCL KEYL=WRKKEYS ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Work with Protocol Table Entries
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=PCLS SCROLL=YES ACTLEN=1 EXTACT=YES.(No entries in table)
:LISTACT OPTION=1 ACTFOR=EXTACT ENTER='CMD ?ADDPCLTBLE PROTOCOL(''&PCLNAME.'')' HELP='WRKPCL/OPTIONS'.1=Add
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD RMVPCLTBLE PROTOCOL(''&PCLNAME.'')' HELP='WRKPCL/OPTIONS'.4=Remove
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='RETURN 105' HELP='WRKPCL/OPTIONS'.5=Display
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='WRKPCL/OPT'.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=SP USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/SP'.
:LISTCOL VAR=PCLNAME USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES MAXWIDTH=38 HELP='FLD/PCLNAME'.Protocol
:LISTCOL VAR=PCLNBR USAGE=OUTPUT MAXWIDTH=8 HELP='FLD/PCLNBR'.Protocol number 
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters for options 1 and 4 or command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKPCLD HELP=HLPPCL KEYL=WRKKEYS ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Work with Protocol Table Entries
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=PCLS SCROLL=YES ACTLEN=1 EXTACT=YES.(No entries in table)
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='RETURN 105' HELP='WRKPCLD/OPTIONS'.5=Display
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='WRKPCLD/OPT'.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=SP USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/SP'.
:LISTCOL VAR=PCLNAME USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES MAXWIDTH=38 HELP='FLD/PCLNAME'.Protocol
:LISTCOL VAR=PCLNBR USAGE=OUTPUT MAXWIDTH=8 HELP='FLD/PCLNBR'.Protocol number 
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters for options 1 and 4 or command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKNET HELP=HLPNET KEYL=WRKKEYS ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Work with Network Table Entries
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=NETS SCROLL=YES ACTLEN=1 EXTACT=YES.(No entries in table)
:LISTACT OPTION=1 ACTFOR=EXTACT ENTER='CMD ?ADDNETTBLE NETWORK(''&NETNAME.'') INTNETADR(''&NETADR.'')' HELP='WRKNET/OPTIONS'.1=Add
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD RMVNETTBLE NETWORK(''&NETNAME.'')' HELP='WRKNET/OPTIONS'.4=Remove
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='RETURN 105' HELP='WRKNET/OPTIONS'.5=Display
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='WRKNET/OPT'.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=SP USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/SP'.
:LISTCOL VAR=NETNAME USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES MAXWIDTH=38 HELP='FLD/NETNAME'.Network
:LISTCOL VAR=NETADR USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES HELP='FLD/NETADR'.Internet address
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters for options 1 and 4 or command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKNETD HELP=HLPNET KEYL=WRKKEYS ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Work with Network Table Entries
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=NETS SCROLL=YES ACTLEN=1 EXTACT=YES.(No entries in table)
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='RETURN 105' HELP='WRKNETD/OPTIONS'.5=Display
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='WRKNETD/OPT'.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=SP USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/SP'.
:LISTCOL VAR=NETNAME USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES MAXWIDTH=38 HELP='FLD/NETNAME'.Network
:LISTCOL VAR=NETADR USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES HELP='FLD/NETADR'.Internet address
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters for options 1 and 4 or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPSRV.Work with Service Table Entries - Help
:P.Each service name with its port and protocol, as programs look them
up by name. Type 4 next to an entry to remove it; option 1 adds one.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPPCL.Work with Protocol Table Entries - Help
:P.Each protocol name with its number.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPNET.Work with Network Table Entries - Help
:P.Each network name with its address.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/WRKKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F6=Print list
:PD.Print list.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F17=Top
:PD.Moves to the top of the list.
:PT.F18=Bottom
:PD.Moves to the bottom of the list.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSRV/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SVCNAME'.Service
:P.The service of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SVCPORT'.Port
:P.The TCP or UDP port number.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SVCPROTO'.Protocol
:P.The protocol of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSRV/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Add
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to add it. The Add Service
Table Entry (ADDSRVTBLE) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.4=Remove
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to remove it. The Remove
Service Table Entry (RMVSRVTBLE) command runs for the entry.
:PT.5=Display
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSRVD/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSRVD/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.5=Display
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKPCL/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SP'.SP
:P.The SP of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PCLNAME'.Protocol
:P.The protocol of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PCLNBR'.Protocol number
:P.The protocol number of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKPCL/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Add
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to add it. The Add Protocol
Table Entry (ADDPCLTBLE) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.4=Remove
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to remove it. The Remove
Protocol Table Entry (RMVPCLTBLE) command runs for the entry.
:PT.5=Display
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKPCLD/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKPCLD/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.5=Display
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKNET/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/NETNAME'.Network
:P.The network of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/NETADR'.Internet address
:P.An internet address in dotted decimal form (IPv4) or in colon form
(IPv6).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKNET/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Add
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to add it. The Add Network
Table Entry (ADDNETTBLE) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.4=Remove
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to remove it. The Remove
Network Table Entry (RMVNETTBLE) command runs for the entry.
:PT.5=Display
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKNETD/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKNETD/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.5=Display
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
